WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.001 line:92%
-Happy Friday, everybody.

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:02.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
Guys, the midterm elections
are coming up.

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:03.737 line:92%
And I saw that by election day,

00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:08.775
President Trump will have spoken
at over 30 rallies in 5 weeks.

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:10.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
The media says
that's a lot of time

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:11.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
to spend away
from the White House,

00:00:11.745 --> 00:00:14.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
or as White House staffers
put it, "Shut up."

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:16.816 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:19.152 line:92%
"Let him -- Let him play."

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:20.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, I read
that Trump is planning

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:23.390 size:84% position:42%
to hold 10 more rallies
before November 6th.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:25.558
If he gets tired,
they're just going to put a wig

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:28.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
on an air horn
and hope nobody notices.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:29.829 size:81% position:41% line:92%
[ Imitating air horn ]

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:32.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Air horn blows ]
Thank you.

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:35.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
I saw that Trump
actually scheduled a rally

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:36.836 size:88% position:44% line:92%
in Florida on Halloween.

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:39.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's giving out tickets by
saying it's a live performance

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.207 size:84% position:42% line:92%
of "The Great Pumpkin."

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:43.076 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:46.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the midterms
are just 11 days away.

00:00:46.513 --> 00:00:50.750
Yeah, 11 days, or as Trump
calls that, just one Scaramucci.

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:54.054 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:55.555 line:92%
I read that Democrats are hoping

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:57.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
that their support
for legal weed

00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:58.958 line:92%
will help them at the polls.

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:00.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know how confident
you can feel

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:03.396
when your strategy relies
on stoners remembering to vote.

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:07.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like, "Is that --
Is that tomorrow?

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:11.104 line:92%
November 29th, man, I'm there."

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:14.140 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:16.643 size:84% position:42% line:92%
"Isn't that Christmas?"

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:19.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
I heard that Utah
might legalize marijuana.

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:23.750
So, a state lawmaker went
to Nevada to research weed.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.718 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:26.519 line:92%
When asked what he learned,

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:28.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
his staff said,
"That was four days ago.

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:28.855 size:78% position:39% line:92%
He hasn't come back."

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:32.859
He's like, "I'll be right there
November 29th."

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:34.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
As I mentioned,
the midterms are coming up,

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:37.697
and Americans are more divided
than ever about who to vote for.

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:39.999
So we thought, what if we
can combine candidates

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:43.002 align:start size:94% position:6%
to create one candidate
that everyone can agree on?

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:43.770 line:92%
I'll show you what I mean.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:47.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
For example, if you combine
Missouri Republican Noga Sachs

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
with Tennessee Republican
Jody Ball,

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:51.377 size:84% position:42% line:92%
they become Ball Sachs.

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:54.214 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:58.885 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Next up, if you combine

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:01.788
California Green Party candidate
Barry Hermanson

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:04.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
with Michigan Democrat
Debbie Dingell,

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:06.192 line:92%
they become Dingell Barry.

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:07.427 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:09.362 line:92%
Everyone can relate to these.

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:11.231 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
If you combine --

00:02:11.231 --> 00:02:12.932 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:16.069
If you combine
Illinois Republican Jaye DeBates

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:18.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Pennsylvania Republican
Kurt Masser,

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:21.007 line:92%
they become Masser DeBates.

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:22.342 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you.

00:02:22.342 --> 00:02:25.678 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:26.613 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-DeBates.

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:28.148 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-If you --

00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:30.683 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:33.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now you're all playing along.
Here we go right now.

00:02:33.186 --> 00:02:37.824
Finally, if you combine
Colorado Republican Peter Yu...

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:39.192 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay.

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:41.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...and Maryland Democrat
Bill Frick,

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:42.695 size:78% position:39% line:92%
they become Frick Yu.

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:46.332
I'm just saying, these are all
candidates we can all agree on.

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:49.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
We can all vote for
and come together.

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:50.103 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Listen to this.

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:51.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you guys hear
that the Vatican

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:53.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
just launched
a new game for kids

00:02:53.006 --> 00:02:56.876
that's like "Pokémon GO" where
you actually collect saints.

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:57.677 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh.

00:02:57.677 --> 00:03:00.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
-When asked if it's as fun
as "Pokémon GO,"

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:01.848 size:78% position:39% line:92%
kids were like, "No."

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:03.016 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:05.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it turns out that's not
the only video game

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:06.119 size:81% position:41% line:92%
that the Vatican made.

00:03:06.119 --> 00:03:09.322
They also released a special
Pope edition of Super Mario.

00:03:09.322 --> 00:03:13.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
Check this thing out.
[ Video game music plays ]

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:16.729 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Uh-oh.

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:18.932 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Oh. Wait.

00:03:18.932 --> 00:03:21.201 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
What?

00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:22.068 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
There's the smoke.

00:03:22.068 --> 00:03:24.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
We got a new pope.
There it is.

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:26.472 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Fantastic game.

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:30.009
Once can see the smoke, that
means you cleared the level.

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:30.910 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-You have a new pope.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:32.145 line:92%
-This is going viral, guys.

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:34.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
Someone took a video
of two corgis

00:03:34.314 --> 00:03:36.015 line:92%
working out on a treadmill.

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:36.616 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Did you see this?

00:03:36.616 --> 00:03:39.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
Two corgi dogs
are working out at a gym.

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:40.453 line:92%
But I'm not sure they were both

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:42.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
putting in the same amount
of effort.

00:03:42.789 --> 00:03:44.457 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Watch this.

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:51.898 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:53.967 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That dude like...

00:03:55.635 --> 00:03:59.439
As long as the Fitbit's
on that paw, it totally counts.

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:01.441 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Counts as a step.

